.TH SDL_Time 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_Time \- SDL times are signed, 64-bit integers representing nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (Jan 1, 1970).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef Sint64 SDL_Time;
.BI "#define SDL_MAX_TIME SDL_MAX_SINT64
.BI "#define SDL_MIN_TIME SDL_MIN_SINT64
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
They can be converted between POSIX time_t values with
.BR SDL_NS_TO_SECONDS ()
and
.BR SDL_SECONDS_TO_NS (),
and between Windows FILETIME values with
.BR SDL_TimeToWindows ()
and
.BR SDL_TimeFromWindows ()\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_MAX_SINT64 (3),
.BR SDL_MIN_SINT64 (3)
